  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Four gases, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> have critical temperatures <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>33</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>126</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>154</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively</p><p>For their adsorption on a fixed amount of charcoal, the correct order is :</p>"
  },
